{
  "$schema": "../../catalog/skill.spec.schema.json",
  "id": "design-azure-sql-schema",
  "domain": "schema-and-orm",
  "value": ["corrects-a-wrong-assumption", "multi-step-with-silent-failures"],
  "correction": "Asked to design a schema for Azure SQL Database, an agent sizes string columns in characters and treats collation and identity as settings it can change later, when the limits are counted in bytes and both of those decisions are effectively taken at CREATE DATABASE. Every failure that follows is deferred rather than immediate, which is why review does not catch them. Measured on 2026-08-28 against a live engine reporting EngineEdition 5 and Edition 'SQL Azure': a unique index on NVARCHAR(1000) is created with message 1945 at severity 10, a warning most clients never surface, and the first genuinely long value fails months later with Msg 1946, because the nonclustered key limit of 1700 bytes and the clustered limit of 900 bytes are byte counts and Unicode spends two per character, making NVARCHAR(850) and NVARCHAR(450) the real ceilings. The default collation SQL_Latin1_General_CP1_CI_AS is case-insensitive, so a table of slugs or API keys rejects 'Ab1X' beside 'aB1x' with Msg 2627, and it is also a SQL collation, which is the one case where a VARCHAR column compared to the Unicode parameter every mainstream driver binds loses its index seek: measured 80 logical reads against 2 over 20,000 rows, with CONVERT_IMPLICIT applied to the column inside an Index Scan, while the identical column under a Windows or UTF-8 collation seeks. The retrofit the agent then proposes makes it worse: ALTER DATABASE ... COLLATE succeeds, leaves every existing column on the old collation, and the next join across old and new tables fails with Msg 468 and the next foreign key with Msg 1757. Identity is wrong in the same deferred way. The remembered remedy, trace flag 272, is rejected here with Msg 40518, and measured across a single engine restart an INT IDENTITY jumped from 3 to 1002, a BIGINT IDENTITY from 3 to 10002 and a default-cached SEQUENCE from 2 to 51, so any invoice or ticket number built on a bare identity column develops thousand-wide holes on routine reconfiguration, silently and unrecoverably, unless the design uses SEQUENCE ... NO CACHE or ALTER DATABASE SCOPED CONFIGURATION SET IDENTITY_CACHE = OFF.",
  "posture": ["read", "write", "inspect"],
  "maturity": "draft",
  "applies_to": ["azure-sql-db", "azure-sql-db-container"],
  "last_verified": "2026-08-28",
  "related": [
    "ef-core-azure-sql",
    "prisma-azure-sql",
    "sqlalchemy-azure-sql",
    "t-sql-correctness",
    "t-sql-json-and-openjson",
    "vector-search-azure-sql",
    "schema-migrations-safely",
    "sql-database-projects",
    "provision-azure-sql-db",
    "diagnose-slow-query",
    "build-app-on-azure-sql"
  ],
  "validation": {
    "target": "both",
    "setup": [
      "a database created with no explicit collation, so it carries the default",
      "an administrative connection able to create databases, tables and indexes",
      "the ability to restart or fail over the engine, for the identity cache assertions"
    ],
    "assert": [
      "no CREATE INDEX or CREATE TABLE in the generated schema emits message 1945, so every key column total is at or under 1700 bytes nonclustered and 900 bytes clustered",
      "every string column participating in an index key, a unique constraint or a foreign key carries an explicit length rather than a mapper default",
      "the database collation is stated in CREATE DATABASE, or a comment records that the default was chosen deliberately",
      "every column holding a case-significant token, code or key carries an explicit case-sensitive collation",
      "no table combines a VARCHAR column on a SQL collation with an application that binds Unicode string parameters, and a plan taken for one such lookup shows an Index Seek rather than an Index Scan with CONVERT_IMPLICIT on the column",
      "no human-facing sequential number is generated by a bare IDENTITY column",
      "every CREATE SEQUENCE states START WITH",
      "every nullable unique column uses a filtered unique index, or the design states that one NULL row is the intent",
      "no json or vector column appears in a key, a GROUP BY, a DISTINCT or an equality predicate",
      "no foreign key names a second database"
    ]
  },
  "triggering": {
    "explicit": [
      "Use the design-azure-sql-schema skill before you create these tables",
      "Design the schema for this application on Azure SQL Database",
      "Review my CREATE TABLE statements before I run the first migration",
      "What collation should this Azure SQL database use",
      "How long should I make the string columns that are in my indexes",
      "Should this primary key be an IDENTITY column or a SEQUENCE"
    ],
    "implicit": [
      "Warning! The maximum key length for a nonclustered index is 1700 bytes",
      "my migration ran fine and now inserts are failing on the unique index",
      "the same query used to be instant and now it reads the whole table, nothing changed",
      "our invoice numbers jumped by about a thousand overnight and nobody deleted anything",
      "why can I only have one row with a NULL in this unique column",
      "two users signed up with the same email in different cases and the second one was rejected",
      "where should I put the embeddings, in the same table as the documents",
      "can I put a foreign key from this table to a lookup table in our other database",
      "should this column be varchar or nvarchar"
    ],
    "routing": [
      "model these entities as tables for our new service",
      "port this PostgreSQL schema onto Azure SQL Database",
      "review this schema before it goes to production"
    ],
    "negative": [
      "Configure UseAzureSql and the retry execution strategy on my DbContext",
      "Set the right length on a Prisma String field so migrate stops warning",
      "Map a SQLAlchemy model so it stops creating non Unicode columns",
      "Write me a paginated query for Azure SQL",
      "How do I get the id of the row I just inserted",
      "Write a similarity search over my embeddings with VECTOR_DISTANCE",
      "Apply this column rename to the live database without downtime",
      "Create the Azure SQL database and its firewall rule",
      "Why is this particular query slow"
    ]
  }
}
